![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

The `timeout` option in `vm.Script.runInContext` only applies to synchronous execution. Since the script is wrapped in an async IIFE, `runInContext` returns a Promise almost immediately, and the `await` on this line will wait for that Promise to settle. If the user-provided script contains an infinite async loop or a non-settling Promise, the runner will hang indefinitely. You should race the script execution against a host-side timeout.

```suggestion
  const timeoutPromise = new Promise((_, reject) =>
    setTimeout(() => reject(new Error("Script execution timed out after " + timeoutMs + "ms")), timeoutMs)
  );
  await Promise.race([script.runInContext(context, { timeout: timeoutMs }), timeoutPromise]);
```

