Attaching listeners to `process.on("SIGINT")` and `process.on("SIGTERM")` inside the command handler can lead to listener leaks if `runMockCommand` is invoked multiple times within the same process (e.g., during integration tests). It is better to use a named cleanup function and remove the listeners once the promise resolves.

```typescript
    return new Promise((resolve) => {
        const cleanup = async () => {
            process.off("SIGINT", cleanup);
            process.off("SIGTERM", cleanup);
            await mock.stop();
            resolve(0);
        };
        process.on("SIGINT", cleanup);
        process.on("SIGTERM", cleanup);
    });
```

