![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)

The `fetch` call in the middleware does not have a timeout. When `fireAndForget` is set to `false`, this can block the main API response indefinitely if the watchfn server is slow. Even when `fireAndForget` is `true`, hanging requests can consume system resources. A short timeout (e.g., 2 seconds) is recommended for telemetry events.

```typescript
            const res = await fetch(eventUrl, {
                method: "POST",
                headers,
                body: JSON.stringify(event),
                signal: AbortSignal.timeout(2000),
            });
```
